/// Spoken on first launch, and from More › Play tutorial.
enum Tutorial {
    static let lines = [
        "Welcome to SightSense. Wear the phone on your chest, upright, with the back camera facing forward.",
        "The screen has three wide bands. Top: Describe what's in front of you. Middle: Ask, to ask a question or say a command. Bottom: Read text, and I'll help you aim.",
        "Along the bottom edge are three buttons. Left corner: Mode, which goes from Navigation to Calm to Live. Middle: beeps on or off. Right corner: More, for places, settings, and help.",
        "Tap Ask and just talk to me: ask a question, or tell me what you need, like: take me to the door. I watch through the camera and answer right away. In Live mode you don't even need to tap; tap Ask to mute me or unmute.",
        "You don't need the screen while the phone is on your chest. Press volume down, or click your AirPods, to ask. Press once and speak, or hold it while you talk. Volume up describes the scene.",
        "Try asking: show me the way out, and I'll guide you to the door with sound. Or: where am I, read this, or any question like: is there an empty seat? Press and hold Ask for a list of quick questions.",
        "Press and hold anywhere on the screen to stop me talking. Swipe up for what's ahead, down for what's around you, left or right for fewer or more announcements.",
        "I only speak up about what matters right now, like something in your path as you walk. Beeps play only while you're walking, and stop when you stand still.",
        "When something is in your way, you'll hear a double beep, feel two buzzes, and hear a short phrase, like: Chair, ahead, 2 steps. A falling tone means the ground drops ahead. A rising tone means something is coming toward you fast.",
        "Everything I say is in this one voice. If the internet drops, you'll hear two low notes; I go quiet, but obstacle warnings keep beeping and buzzing until I'm back.",
        "SightSense helps, but it can miss things. Always keep using your cane or guide dog.",
        "In Settings, set your chest height for accurate distances.",
    ]
}
